Package: tidyagsim
Title: Tidymodels-Style Tuning and Replication for Agricultural Simulations
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Jay", "Gillenwater", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "55106933+jhgille2@users.noreply.github.com"))
Description: Brings the grammar of the 'tidymodels' packages to stochastic
    simulation studies in plant breeding. Mark the arguments of a simulation
    with tune(), describe replicate seeds and assumption scenarios, choose a
    metric set, and let grid search, racing or Bayesian optimization run the
    experiment without enumerating every combination by hand. Results are tidy
    tibbles with Monte Carlo standard errors, and helpers such as show_best()
    and select_by_one_std_err() pick designs. Includes a fast simulator for
    QTL mapping populations (F2, recombinant inbred lines, BCsFt, nested
    association mapping, advanced-backcross NAM and MAGIC) and an engine for
    'breedsim' breeding-program flowcharts.
